{"title":"SkyLine MRO","sub":"Why do aircraft spend so long in maintenance?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Aviation","geo":"Europe","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"30 min","skills":"Process mapping · finding waiting time · cost-benefit","prompt":"SkyLine is a mid-sized airline with 40 narrow-body aircraft. Every two years each aircraft goes through a 'heavy check', a major maintenance overhaul done in SkyLine's own hangar. A heavy check takes 28 days, versus 20 days at the best airlines. The COO wants to know why, and what it's worth to fix.","clarify":[{"q":"Why does time matter?","a":"An aircraft in the hangar can't fly. Each lost day costs about $60,000 of contribution."},{"q":"Volume?","a":"40 aircraft, each checked every 2 years → 20 heavy checks a year."},{"q":"Quality issues?","a":"No. Safety and quality are fine; it's only about time."}],"structure":{"root":"Why 28 days, and what's it worth?","branches":[{"head":"Size the prize","items":["Days lost × checks × cost per day"]},{"head":"Map the process","items":["Inspection","Waiting for parts","Repair work","Approvals","Testing & release"]},{"head":"Levers","items":["People: shifts, skills","Process: parallel work, kitting","Technology: digital sign-off, parts forecasting"]}]},"hypothesis":"The repair work itself is probably similar to the best airlines; the extra days are likely waiting time.","questions":[{"q":"What is the prize if SkyLine matches the best airlines?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>8 days × 20 checks × $60k = <b>$9.6M a year</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Here's where the 28 days go. What do you see?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"389.32pt\" height=\"209.744pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 389.32 209.744\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 209.744 L 389.32 209.744 L 389.32 0 L 0 0 L 0 